# X-22 -- the N-bit LK covariance cost curve, reference device (pi4)
#
# FOUR RUNS, IN THREE DIFFERENT BINARIES. Read the caveat before quoting any
# absolute ns figure out of this file.
#
#   RUN 1  benchmark/covariance_nbit_benchmark.cpp with FIVE arms -- the shipped
#          kernel only (ternary + bit-sliced N=1..4). This source is not the one in
#          the tree: the four `window-acc` arms were added afterwards.
#   RUN 2  the committed source, NINE arms. This is the run X-22's tables quote.
#   RUN 3  the SAME BINARY as run 2, re-run, to separate code layout from run-to-run
#          noise. It reproduces run 2 to ~1% on every row.
#   RUN 4  the nine arms again after the T3.10 triage removed dead work from the
#          per-row accumulator's add(). A third binary; see its own header.
#
# Runs 2 and 3 agree to ~1%; run 1 disagrees with both by up to 46% on arms whose
# SOURCE did not change (uint64_t, N=3, W=31: 4652.6 ns in run 1 against 6803.4 and
# 6771.5 ns in runs 2 and 3). Same device, same governor, same pinning, clean
# throttle state throughout all three. What differs is the number of template
# instantiations in one translation unit -- the code-layout effect
# benchmark/morphology_path_benchmark.cpp already recorded at ~10%, here at up to
# 1.46x. So: within a binary this benchmark is reproducible to ~1%, and between
# binaries the same kernel's absolute cost moves by up to ~1.5x. X-22's conclusions
# are written against that, and T4.1 must re-measure in its own binary rather than
# quote a number from this one.
#
# Environment (identical for all four runs):
#   device:           pi4
#   cpu:              Raspberry Pi 4 Model B Rev 1.5
#   arch / kernel:    aarch64 / 6.18.34+rpt-rpi-v8
#   compiler:         g++ (Debian 14.2.0-19) 14.2.0
#   governor:         performance (restored to ondemand on exit)
#   core pinning:     taskset -c 3
#   throttled before: throttled=0x0
#   throttled after:  throttled=0x0
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RUN 1 -- five arms, shipped kernel only (source not in the tree)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
